{
  "scenario_name": "maian_vehicle_boost_smoke",
  "description": "Maian vehicle V3 (Mike 2026-11-16): boost and heat. The Maian hover vehicle mod (built by the in-game mod author from dev-mods/maian_hover_vehicle/recipe.json, with behavior/variables.json, pd.vehicle_variables.v1) replaces CI training's hoverbike and is driven. Holding the new mappable boost action (ACTION_VEHICLE_BOOST, Shift / controller A) ramps the boost to full in about 1 s; after about 4 s of boost the crystals overheat: the seafoam crystal part (140) is hidden so the black ones inside it show, boost drops to its cap, steering is limited briefly and the turret is locked (logged until V5 reads it); letting go recovers the crystals in 2 to 4 s depending on speed. Runs on Escape (--launch-mission base:escape). The mount hook places Player 0 beside the bike with chrMoveToPos, which now skips the body model a solo player does not have outside a cutscene (B-1158; the hook used to wait for that model, which never came, so it never mounted on any campaign stage). Escape starts with the player pushing the hover bed (grab mode, as in the original; B-1159, not a bug): after the intro is skipped, one direct-activate press (ACTION_VEHICLE_USE, E) lets go of it, and the mount hook, which waits for walk mode, fires. Screenshots: full boost, black crystals, recovering, cool.",
  "tags": [
    "vehicle",
    "modding",
    "mod-author",
    "pdvehicle",
    "recipe",
    "gameplay",
    "maian-vehicle",
    "vehicle-boost",
    "pillar:modding"
  ],
  "paths_of_interest": [
